{
  "summary": "Bumps the minimum supported GCC compiler version from 12.1 to 13.1, enforcing C++20 `std::format` support during CMake configuration. It updates CI environments to use GCC 13 and Ubuntu 24.04, removes the NetBSD cross-build job from the GitHub Actions matrix, and replaces an example `strprintf` invocation with `std::format` in a benchmark.",
  "problem": "GCC 12 lacks support for C++20 `std::format`, preventing developers from using standard text formatting across the codebase and blocking the project's eventual migration to C++23.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"For this bump, only C++20 `std::format` will become available, but this bump should also pave the way for C++23.\"",
    "Commit ee8d04cd15 demonstrates the payoff by migrating `src/bench/wallet_migration.cpp` from `tinyformat` (`strprintf`) to `std::format`."
  ],
