  "card": "PR 36042 raises the minimum supported GCC compiler version from 12.1 to 13.1, enforced in CMake via a feature check for C++20 std::format. This enables codebase adoption of std::format and paves the way for C++23, while requiring users on older Linux distributions lacking GCC 13 to build using Clang or alternative toolchains. CI configurations are updated to Ubuntu 24.04, and the NetBSD cross-compilation task is removed from GitHub Actions.",
